TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_CataTweaks_CouncilSize7=Deep Cover Handlers
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_CataTweaks_CouncilSize7=A seventh seat, paid for out of the budget that ran an agent in someone else's council.
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_CataTweaks_CouncilSize7=Running an asset inside a rival council was never cheap. A handler, a cut-out, a courier route that has to survive its own success, and a case officer whose entire working life is one person who might be lying. Covert Operations taught us to sustain two of them at once. This teaches us what the ledger has been saying all along: that the same apparatus, turned inward and given a name badge, seats another of our own people at our own table. We are not recruiting a spy. We are spending the spy on ourselves.
TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_CataTweaks_CouncilSize8=Shadow Cabinet
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_CataTweaks_CouncilSize8=An eighth seat, and the last of the handlers comes in from the cold.
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_CataTweaks_CouncilSize8=Every council keeps a second council: the people who would take over if the first one were arrested, discredited, or vaporized. Ours has been meeting in safe houses and paying for itself out of the intelligence line, which is a tidy arrangement until the day it is needed and nobody can find it. So we seat it. The last handler surrenders their network, the last cut-out is stood down, and the chair that funded a listening post in a rival's cabinet is carried upstairs and set at the head of the table. Nothing is now hidden from us that we did not choose to stop watching.
TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_TheSunNeverSets=The Sun Never Sets
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_TheSunNeverSets=Reassert claims on the thirteen colonies, the Caribbean, British India and selected European crowns.
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_TheSunNeverSets=Commonwealth Restored brought back the settler dominions. Now we turn to the thirteen colonies, the Caribbean islands and British India, including Burma. In Europe, the Crown invokes its dynastic connections: France, Germany, Spain, Portugal, the Low Countries, Scandinavia, Greece, Romania and European Russia. The claim ends at these shores and crowns; it is not a mandate for the rest of the former Empire. We file the paperwork, and let the rest follow. In Broken Earth, completing this project also makes our starting claims on Jamaica and Ireland peaceful.
TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_NewLiberia=New Liberia
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_NewLiberia=Monrovia, Freetown and Libreville: one coast, one founding idea.
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_NewLiberia=Three powers had the same notion within forty years of each other, and none of them thought to compare notes. The Americans put freed slaves ashore at Monrovia, the British at Freetown, the French at Libreville - the free town, in case the point was missed. Between them lies the Kru coast, whose sailors crewed the ships that carried all three. The descendants of those settlements have more in common with each other than with the empires that dropped them here, and they have started saying so.
TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_MareNostrum=All Roads Lead to Rome
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_MareNostrum=Broad claims in continental Europe, including European Russia. +10 control point capacity.
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_MareNostrum=Grants territorial claims throughout continental Europe, including European Russia for incremental conquest. New foreign claims are hostile. Claims on the Italian core are peaceful. Requires Great Nations and is independent of the other Roman regional projects. Completing this project grants the researching faction +10 control point capacity. Available only in Broken Earth.
TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_CataTweaks_RomanAfrica=Scipio’s Legacy
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_CataTweaks_RomanAfrica=Broad claims in Africa and its adjacent islands. +10 control point capacity.
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_CataTweaks_RomanAfrica=Grants territorial claims throughout Africa and its adjacent islands for incremental conquest. New foreign claims are hostile. Requires Great Nations and is independent of the other Roman regional projects. Completing this project grants the researching faction +10 control point capacity. Available only in Broken Earth.
TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_CataTweaks_RomanIndia=Beyond Alexander
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_CataTweaks_RomanIndia=Broad claims in the Indian subcontinent, including Pakistan, Bangladesh, Nepal, Bhutan, Sri Lanka and the Maldives. +10 control point capacity.
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_CataTweaks_RomanIndia=Grants territorial claims throughout the Indian subcontinent, including Pakistan, Bangladesh, Nepal, Bhutan, Sri Lanka and the Maldives for incremental conquest. New foreign claims are hostile. Requires Great Nations and is independent of the other Roman regional projects. Completing this project grants the researching faction +10 control point capacity. Available only in Broken Earth.
